      ],
      "explanation": "\\((x+3)(x-3)=x^2-9\\). When \\(x=5\\), its value is \\(25-9=16\\).",
      "id": "conjugate-product",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_147_q3#conjugate-product",
      "title": "Difference of squares"
    },
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_146",
        "cnm_034",
        "cnm_037"
      ],
      "explanation": "Multiplying each term in the first factor by each term in the second shows why the middle terms cancel:\n\\[\n(x+3)(x-3)=x^2-3x+3x-9=x^2-9.\n\\]\nWhen \\(x=5\\), the value is \\(5^2-9=16\\). Thus the simplified expression is \\(x^2-9\\), and its requested value is \\(16\\).",
      "id": "distribute-and-cancel",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_147_q3#distribute-and-cancel",
      "title": "Expand and cancel the middle terms"
    }
